# What must not enter this stage's build context.
#
# The same list ships in every one of this task's stage directories -- a stage
# that excluded something the others kept would produce an image nobody could
# reproduce from the tree.
#
# Every cache pattern is `**/`-prefixed on purpose.  A .dockerignore pattern is
# matched against the whole context-relative path and is *not* applied at every
# depth the way a .gitignore pattern is, so a bare `__pycache__/` excludes only a
# `__pycache__` sitting at the context root -- it does not exclude
# `lib/__pycache__` or `modules/closure/__pycache__`, which are the only places
# this suite ever produces one.  Without the prefix the host's bytecode is copied
# into the image: interpreter-tagged .pyc files compiled by whatever Python and
# pytest the author happened to run, shipped alongside a pinned 3.11 and pytest
# 8.3.4 that will never load them.  They are dead weight in the best case and a
# stale module in the worst, and PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE in the Dockerfile does
# not help -- it stops the *image* writing bytecode, not the COPY bringing it in.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*~
**/*.orig
**/*.rej
**/.DS_Store

# The metadata inspector is built inside the image, from source, by the pinned
# SDK.  A host-built bin/ or obj/ would be another compiler's output smuggled in
# -- and `dotnet build` would then decide it had nothing to do.  Only
# tests/behavioural/ actually holds the .csproj: in the other stage directories
# these two lines match nothing, and are kept so all three copies stay identical.
#
# Named by path rather than as `**/obj`, which is what this file said first and
# which cost a build: `**/obj` matches ANY path element called obj, and one of the
# twenty module directories is `modules/obj` -- the family of cases about jsonnet
# objects.  Excluding it dropped a module the suite declares, and the build failed
# on `suite.toml names missing module dir(s): ['obj']`.  The `**/` prefix above is
# right for __pycache__, which appears wherever a module happens to be imported
# from; it is wrong here, because build output appears only beside a .csproj and
# there is exactly one of those.
lib/asminspect/bin
lib/asminspect/obj
